<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Evidence review — {{ preview.case_id }}</title>{% include 'browser_style.html.j2' %}</head>
<body>
<header><span class="badge">Before the LLM</span><h1>Review parsed evidence</h1>
<p><strong>{{ preview.case_id }}</strong> · Evidence version {{ preview.evidence_version }} · As of {{ evidence.as_of_date }} · Cutoff {{ evidence.evidence_cutoff_timestamp }}</p>
<ol class="workflow"><li>Uploaded</li><li>Cutoff checked</li><li>Parsed and mapped</li><li>Metrics calculated</li><li class="current">Evidence review</li><li class="pending">LLM pending</li></ol>
<p class="notice">Processing has stopped at this review point. LLM calls: <strong>{{ preview.llm_calls }}</strong>. Parsed facts and candidate passages retain their evidence quality and review requirements.</p>
<div class="actions"><a href="/inspect">Upload another file</a><a href="/">All cases</a><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/payload.json">Full preview JSON</a><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/llm-input.json">Next LLM input JSON</a><a href="/cases/{{ preview.case_id }}/workbench.html">Case workbench</a></div>
</header>
<nav><ul><li><a href="#outputs">Saved outputs / JSON</a></li><li><a href="#sources">Sources and cutoff</a></li><li><a href="#facts">Facts</a></li><li><a href="#metrics">Available metrics</a></li><li><a href="#narrative">Text / narrative</a></li><li><a href="#sec">SEC diagnostics</a></li><li><a href="#issues">Review issues</a></li><li><a href="#llm">LLM boundary</a></li></ul></nav>
<main>
<section id="outputs"><h2>Saved outputs and JSON downloads</h2><p>Inspect the saved admission results, extracted and mapped evidence, reconciled values, calculations and prepared LLM input. New runs record extraction and mapping separately; combined views are also retained.</p>
<p class="subtle">{{ manifest.origin }}</p>
<p><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/artifacts.json">Open the export manifest and checksums</a></p>
{% if reference_checks %}<p class="notice">Reference checks: {{ reference_checks.passed }} / {{ reference_checks.total }} source-value and metric checks passed. Scanned-document numeric recognition: {{ reference_checks.ocr_recognition.recognized_reference_cells }} / {{ reference_checks.ocr_recognition.reference_cells }} visually transcribed cells matched ({{ '%.1f' | format(reference_checks.ocr_recognition.fraction * 100) }}%). This measures page-level numeric recognition, not semantic verification.</p><details><summary>OCR values needing attention</summary><pre>{{ reference_checks.ocr_recognition | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details>{% endif %}
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Saved output</th><th>Download</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for artifact in manifest.artifacts %}<tr><td>{{ artifact.label }}</td><td><a href="{{ artifact.url }}">JSON</a><br><small>{{ artifact.size_bytes }} bytes</small></td><td class="hash">{{ artifact.sha256 }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and cutoff</h2><p>{{ evidence.documents | length }} admitted files · {{ preview.rejected_sources | length }} rejected files.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Parser / role</th><th>Available at</th><th>Original SHA-256</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for doc in evidence.documents %}<tr id="doc-{{ doc.document_id }}"><td><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/sources/{{ doc.document_id }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ doc.filename }}</a></td><td>{{ doc.role | default(doc.parser) }}</td><td>{{ doc.available_at }}</td><td class="hash">{{ doc.sha256 }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<h3>Document extraction coverage</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Readable pages</th><th>OCR pages</th><th>Captured characters / numeric tokens</th><th>Failed pages</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for doc in evidence.documents %}{% if doc.extraction_coverage is defined %}{% set coverage = doc.extraction_coverage %}<tr><td>{{ doc.filename }}</td><td>{{ coverage.readable_pages }} / {{ coverage.total_pages }}</td><td>{{ coverage.ocr_pages }}</td><td>{{ coverage.characters }} / {{ coverage.numeric_tokens }}</td><td>{{ coverage.failed_pages | join(', ') or 'None' }}</td></tr>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div><p class="subtle">Coverage counts retained text and numeric tokens. It does not imply that every number is mapped or that OCR is accurate. Full page text, OCR boxes and raw numeric candidates are downloadable in the document artifacts.</p>
{% for doc in preview.rejected_sources %}<p class="notice"><strong>Excluded: {{ doc.filename }}</strong> · {{ doc.available_at }}<br>{{ doc.reason }}</p>{% endfor %}
{% if not evidence.documents %}<p class="notice">No source passed the cutoff. Facts, calculations and LLM inputs remain empty or unavailable.</p>{% endif %}
{% for doc in evidence.documents %}{% for note in doc.notes | default([]) %}<p class="notice"><strong>{{ doc.filename }}</strong><br>{{ note }}</p>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
<details><summary>Full admitted source metadata and provenance</summary><pre>{{ evidence.documents | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details></section>
<section id="facts"><h2>Extracted and mapped facts</h2><p>{{ evidence.facts | length }} observations. Inspect raw text, normalized units, periods, dimensions and source references.</p>
{% if evidence.documents and not evidence.facts %}<p class="notice">No structured facts were extracted. Inspect the parser issues and readable text below; this file may need a different format or extraction recipe.</p>{% endif %}
<div class="filter-row"><label for="fact-search">Find a concept, label, period or member</label><input type="search" id="fact-search" placeholder="For example: revenue, Gaming, 2026"><label for="fact-mapping">Mapping</label><select id="fact-mapping"><option value="all">All observations</option><option value="mapped">Mapped</option><option value="unmapped">Unmapped</option><option value="not_financial">Text</option></select><span id="fact-count" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
<div class="table-wrap facts-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Field / original concept</th><th>Raw</th><th>Normalized</th><th>Period</th><th>Dimensions / scope</th><th>Mapping / quality</th><th>Exact source</th></tr></thead><tbody id="fact-rows">
{% for fact in evidence.facts %}<tr data-mapping="{{ fact.mapping_status }}">
<td>{{ fact.name }}<br><small>{{ fact.original_name | default(fact.taxonomy_concept, true) | default('', true) }}</small></td>
<td>{{ (fact.raw_value | string)[:180] if fact.raw_value is not none else 'missing' }}{% if fact.raw_value is string and fact.raw_value | length > 180 %}…{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ fact.normalized_value if fact.normalized_value is not none else 'unavailable' }}<br><small>{{ fact.normalized_unit | default('', true) }}</small></td>
<td>FY {{ fact.fiscal_year | default('?', true) }} · {{ fact.period_type | default('', true) }}<br><small>{{ fact.period_start | default('', true) }} → {{ fact.period_end | default('', true) }}</small></td>
<td>{{ fact.dimensions | tojson if fact.dimensions else 'Dimensionless' }}<br><small>{{ fact.consolidation_scope }}</small></td>
<td>{{ fact.mapping_status }}<br><small>{{ fact.status }} · {{ fact.accounting_basis }} · {{ fact.extraction_method }}</small><br><button type="button" class="review-fact" data-fact="{{ fact.fact_id }}">Review</button></td>
<td>{% for ref in fact.source_refs[:1] %}<a href="#doc-{{ ref.document_id }}">{{ ref.document_id[:12] }}</a>{% if ref.page %}<br><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/sources/{{ ref.document_id }}#page={{ ref.page }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Page {{ ref.page }}</a>{% endif %}{% if ref.table %}<br>{{ ref.table }} · {{ ref.cell }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if fact.xbrl_context_id %}<br>Context {{ fact.xbrl_context_id }}{% endif %}{% if fact.inline_element_id %}<br>Inline {{ fact.inline_element_id }}{% endif %}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<details><summary>Selected canonical values and reconciliation quality</summary><pre>{{ evidence.data_quality | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details></section>
<section id="metrics"><h2>Available calculations</h2><p>{{ metric_review.available | length }} of {{ metric_review.total }} configured metrics can be calculated from this evidence. {{ metric_review.mapped_observations }} of {{ metric_review.total_observations }} extracted observations are mapped.</p>
<p class="subtle">Metrics are calculated from eligible, reconciled inputs; they are not directly parsed rows. The current extraction covers {{ metric_review.extracted_fields | join(', ') }}. Other values may exist in the PDFs without being extracted by this recipe. Configuration is illustrative.</p>
{% if metric_review.available %}<div class="table-wrap"><table id="available-metrics"><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Result</th><th>Period</th><th>Evidence quality</th><th>Review needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for item in metric_review.available %}{% set metric = item.metric %}<tr><td>{{ item.name | replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{% if metric.units == 'ratio' %}{{ '%.2f' | format(metric.result * 100) }}%{% else %}{{ '%.6g' | format(metric.result) }} <small>{{ metric.units }}</small>{% endif %}</td><td>FY {{ metric.fiscal_year }}<br><small>{{ metric.period }}</small></td><td>{{ metric.evidence_quality }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if metric.review_required else 'no' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% else %}<p class="notice">No metric currently has usable inputs. The extracted facts and the missing-input explanations remain available for review.</p>{% endif %}
{% if metric_review.unavailable %}<details id="unavailable-metrics"><summary>{{ metric_review.unavailable | length }} unavailable calculations — inspect missing inputs</summary><p>These outputs are preserved in the saved JSON. Missing inputs can reflect extraction coverage, mapping, reporting periods, scope or unresolved conflicts.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Calculation state</th><th>Reason / required inputs</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for item in metric_review.unavailable %}<tr><td>{{ item.name | replace('_',' ') }}</td><td>{{ item.metric.calculation_state }}</td><td>{{ item.metric.detail | default('Review calculation inputs.', true) }}<br><small>Required: {{ item.required_inputs | join(', ') }}</small>{% for input in item.missing_inputs %}<p><strong>{{ input.name }}</strong>: {{ input.reason }}</p>{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></details>{% endif %}
<details><summary>Full formula inputs, trends and benchmarks</summary><pre>{{ {'metrics':preview.metrics,'trends':preview.trends,'benchmarks':preview.benchmarks} | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details></section>
<section id="narrative"><h2>Readable text and narrative evidence</h2><p>{{ evidence.narrative_evidence | length }} source-grounded candidate passages.</p>
{% for passage in evidence.narrative_evidence %}<details><summary>{{ passage.section }} · {{ passage.candidate_topics | join(', ') if passage.candidate_topics else 'Readable source text' }} · Source {{ passage.document_id[:12] }}</summary><p><strong>{{ passage.heading }}</strong> · {{ passage.evidence_id }}</p><pre>{{ passage.text }}</pre></details>{% else %}<p>No readable narrative passages were extracted for this source.</p>{% endfor %}</section>
<section id="sec"><h2>SEC filing diagnostics</h2>
{% for filing in evidence.sec_filings %}<h3>{{ filing.accession }} · {{ filing.form }}</h3><p>{{ filing.contexts | length }} contexts · {{ filing.observations | length }} observations · {{ filing.presentation | length }} presentation sections · {{ filing.subsidiaries | length }} subsidiary candidates.</p>
{% for key in ['contexts','units','labels','presentation','subsidiaries','warnings','deferred_linkbases'] %}<details><summary>{{ key | replace('_',' ') | capitalize }}</summary><pre>{{ filing[key] | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details>{% endfor %}
{% else %}<p>This source was processed through a PDF, table or standalone XBRL parser.</p>{% endfor %}</section>
<section id="issues"><h2>Items to review</h2><p>{{ preview.mapping_issues | length }} mapping review groups · {{ preview.escalations | length }} escalations.</p>
<details><summary>Mapping review groups and their observations</summary><pre>{{ preview.mapping_issues | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details>
{% for item in preview.escalations %}<details><summary>{{ item.rule_id }}{% if item.mandatory %} · mandatory{% endif %} · {{ item.reason }}</summary><pre>{{ item | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details>{% endfor %}
<details><summary>Evidence coverage and limitations</summary><pre>{{ preview.coverage | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details></section>
<section id="review-controls"><h2>Review evidence</h2><p>Each evidence decision creates a new version, recalculates metrics, and records your reason. Original files, observations and earlier versions remain available.</p><form method="post" action="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/review"><fieldset><legend>Evidence decision</legend><label>Action<select name="action"><option value="verify">Verify a source value / derived definition</option><option value="map">Map an unmapped or ambiguous fact</option><option value="select">Select a source value for a conflict</option></select></label><label>Fact<select name="fact_id" id="review-fact-id" required>{% for fact in evidence.facts if fact.normalized_value is not none %}<option value="{{ fact.fact_id }}">{{ fact.name }} · {{ fact.normalized_value }} {{ fact.normalized_unit }} · {{ fact.period_type }} {{ fact.fiscal_year }} · {{ fact.accounting_basis }} · {{ fact.fact_id[:12] }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label>Canonical name (mapping only)<select name="canonical_name"><option value="">Choose when mapping</option>{% for name in mapping_names %}<option>{{ name }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label>Reconciliation field (choose for a conflict)<select name="field"><option value="">Locate from the selected fact</option>{% for key, quality in evidence.data_quality.items() if quality.state == 'conflicting' %}<option value="{{ key }}">{{ key }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label>Your name<input name="reviewer" required maxlength="120"></label><label>Reason and definition / source check<input name="reason" required maxlength="2000"></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I checked the source and explicitly confirm this decision.</label><button type="submit">Save decision and recalculate</button></fieldset></form>
<h3>Resolve an exception</h3><p>Resolution records a human judgment; it does not change extracted values or remove the exception's history.</p><form method="post" action="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/resolve"><fieldset><label>Open exception<select name="escalation_id" required>{% for issue in live_escalations if issue.status == 'open' %}<option value="{{ issue.escalation_id }}">{{ issue.reason }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label>Your name<input name="reviewer" required maxlength="120"></label><label>Resolution reason<input name="reason" required maxlength="2000"></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I explicitly approve this resolution.</label><button type="submit">Record resolution</button></fieldset></form><h3>Review history</h3>{% for review in reviews %}<details><summary>{{ review.action }} · {{ review.reviewer }} · {{ review.reason }}</summary><pre>{{ {'review_id':review.review_id,'before':review.prior_value,'after':review.new_value} | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></details>{% else %}<p>No recorded reviews.</p>{% endfor %}</section>
<section id="llm"><h2>LLM boundary</h2><p>The next step is qualitative extraction from this canonical evidence snapshot. <a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/llm-input.json">Open the exact prepared input JSON</a> to inspect the payload.</p>
<p>Configured provider: {{ provider }}{% if provider_model %} · Model: {{ provider_model }}{% endif %}. Offline mode exercises the workflow with empty scripted AI outputs. Live mode sends this saved evidence to your configured model.</p><form method="post" action="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/{{ preview.evidence_version }}/continue"><label>Draft mode<select name="mode"><option value="offline">Offline workflow test</option><option value="live">Live configured LLM</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> Generate a draft from this evidence version. Live mode may incur provider charges.</label><label><input type="checkbox" name="rerun" value="yes"> Regenerate as a new draft if one already exists (new model calls in live mode).</label><button type="submit">Generate draft</button></form>{% for draft in drafts %}<p><a href="/inspect/{{ preview.case_id }}/drafts/{{ draft.snapshot_version }}">{{ 'Final' if draft.finalized else 'Draft' }} {{ draft.snapshot_version }}</a></p>{% endfor %}</section>
</main>
<script>
const rows = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#fact-rows tr'));
document.querySelectorAll('.review-fact').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  document.getElementById('review-fact-id').value = button.dataset.fact;
  document.getElementById('review-controls').scrollIntoView();
}));
document.querySelectorAll('form').forEach(form => form.addEventListener('submit', () => {
  const button = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
  if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Processing…'; }
}));
const search = document.getElementById('fact-search');
const mapping = document.getElementById('fact-mapping');
function filterFacts() {
  const term = search.value.trim().toLowerCase(); let count = 0;
  for (const row of rows) { const show = (mapping.value === 'all' || row.dataset.mapping === mapping.value) && row.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(term); row.hidden = !show; if (show) count++; }
  document.getElementById('fact-count').textContent = count + ' shown';
}
search.addEventListener('input',filterFacts); mapping.addEventListener('change',filterFacts); filterFacts();
</script></body></html>
